17592186045417] [17592186272001 #edb/ref 1074 "A vector $u$ belongs to the kernel of a linear transformation $T$ if $T(u)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, we need to compute $T({v}_{i})$ for each vector ${v}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\,T({v}_{2})=0,$ we conclude that the only vector that belongs to the kernel of $\\,T$ is ${v}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321446 #edb/ref 1080 "{[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,z\\in R}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321446 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321446 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26744c84-4da4-549b-b265-e365ea1b2c86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321555 #edb/ref 1080 "${v}_{2}$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321555 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321555 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3542d1a9-0149-5a87-845a-c2a1358d7505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321776 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321776 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321776 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "502cb7bf-d839-54d5-80e3-9ea7df778ed3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321795 #edb/ref 1080 "{[\\begin{aligned}z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,z\\in R}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321795 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321795 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5225c40a-0242-5a8f-b880-4361e75f2a0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321879 #edb/ref 1080 "${v}_{3}$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321879 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321879 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5c7dfa2f-34db-56d